WEBVTT

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:14.040
Wait, Mr. Kazuta!

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.750
Why are you running away?

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:21.370
Wait.

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:23.540
What was that about?

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:28.080
What's up with you?

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:30.080
I found Mr. Kazuta Haruka!

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:32.830
Huh? Kazuta?

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:33.910
Kazuta Haruka?!

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:35.500
That's what I said.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:38.250
He had a hole in his head, but he's alive.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.160
He was in the crowd just now.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:42.580
But when I called to him, he ran off.

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:44.040
What?

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.870
This is an emergency.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:47.540
We need to find him.

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:50.040
Still, I'm surprised he's not dead.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:52.000
Fukuda lived, too.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.200
It's not impossible to survive from a wound like that.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.450
Yeah, you're right.

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:01.160
But what are you so worked up over?

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:02.410
What?

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:36.200
Kazuta Haruka survived, didn't he?

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.700
He conquered his injury.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.120
The same as you.

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:46.200
Even so, his hole and mine aren't the same.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.290
Meaning?

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:52.540
I'm just saying that no two head holes are alike.

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:56.200
See for yourself. Just ask him.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:03:00.080
"Does the wind blowing
through your hole feel cool?"

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:02.790
Is it better if it does?

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:07.790
Speaking from my hole experience,
it means trouble if it's not.

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:12.620
How old are you, again?

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:13.450
Hondomachi.

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:15.040
Oh, yes?

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:16.330
How old are you?

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:19.660
Oh, well, I'm 23.

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:21.500
You're not a middle schooler.

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:24.200
All this over a little smack on the lips?

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:25.330
Oh, no.

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:26.750
That's not it at all.

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:27.660
Come on.

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:30.080
It was just sudden. And odd.

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:33.620
That's not what I was thinking about.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:37.080
I was wondering why Mr. Kazuta was even there.

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:39.870
Hmm. It was a sensational case.

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:42.910
Mostly likely the entire
population of Japan was riveted

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:45.580
to the case for those three days.

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:49.830
Many people also showed up because
they noticed the commotion nearby.

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:53.120
I heard there were roughly
2,000 in that neighborhood.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:55.700
That's the thing, isn't it?

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:57.950
Why <i>there</i>?

00:03:58.910 --> 00:04:05.700
Considering... how the Gravedigger
would feel at first... about having a copycat...

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:08.830
Wait. Wait.

00:04:08.830 --> 00:04:12.370
I mean, you don't actually have to wait... um...

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:14.160
What is it?

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:17.790
This might sound like quite a leap, but...

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.000
Tell me.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:24.200
What if we suppose Kazuta Haruka
wasn't there simply as an onlooker,

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:27.540
but instead was there to check out the copycat?

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:31.700
Okay. Why would he need to do that?

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:33.290
Perhaps...

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:37.540
...because Kazuta Haruka
is the real Gravedigger.

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:38.700
What if that's it?

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:39.660
What?!

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:42.120
That's why he snuck away.

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:44.750
He wasn't acting like an onlooker.

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:48.950
Okay. So then the real Gravedigger just
kissed you after you called out to him?

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:50.250
That's the key.

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:53.290
I was surprised by what he did.

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:56.620
But Kazuta Haruka was also surprised himself.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:05:00.700
That's because it was an unexpected
course of action for him, too.

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:07.160
It was inadvertent?

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:09.660
What would you have done in his shoes?

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:13.580
A police officer stops you at
the scene of your copycat's arrest,

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:15.250
and you can't escape.

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:19.250
Hmm. Well, I would get rid of you, wouldn't I.

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:23.750
No, I'd also want to keep you
from talking, so I'd go further.

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:26.040
That is, you'd try to kill me.

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:30.500
That's the logical choice, and that's
what Kazuta must have meant to do.

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:33.620
What? But he got mixed up?

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:37.660
Mr. Matsuoka, the reason we can't
seem to catch the Gravedigger

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:40.450
is the lack of cognition particles, isn't it?

00:05:40.450 --> 00:05:43.580
Without an id well, the Wellside is paralyzed.

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:44.700
Right.

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:50.200
He kidnaps someone, traps them in a barrel,
and broadcasts them until they suffocate...

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:55.200
He's done it <i>six </i>times. There's no way
the Gravedigger has no drive to kill, right?

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:56.370
Yeah.

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:59.410
Then why haven't we detected it?

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:02.580
Not even at the scene of the kidnapping.

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:06.000
My theory is this:

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:11.330
Inside Kazuta Haruka, the urge to kill could be cross wired with kissing--

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:14.700
with all expressions of love.

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:19.700
Primarily, the head wound caused damage to his brain.

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:22.410
Go to Oono Genpei's house.

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:24.620
Go to where he kissed me!

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:31.750
Unbelievable!

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:33.000
See?

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:36.450
There was no reason for
Kazuta Haruka to kiss me.

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:42.160
The urges to kill and kiss have been
interchanged in his unconscious.

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:46.870
Hey! That means that
asshole was trying to kill me!

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:53.080
My maidenly innocence is a bit
damaged, but this makes up for it!

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:57.200
There's a possibility the Gravedigger's
identity is Kazuta Haruka.

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:59.410
Hondomachi... You...

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:00.750
Yes?

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:02.950
No, nevermind.

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:06.950
Supposing that kisses takes the
place of Kazuta's drive to kill...

00:07:06.950 --> 00:07:08.500
He said "kisses."

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:13.450
Does that mean when we corner
him, he'll attack with kisses?

00:07:14.290 --> 00:07:17.500
No, most likely not.

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:20.660
An impulse is just the impetus for action,

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:25.950
so if he puts some conscious thought into
killing someone, I'm sure he can do it.

00:07:25.950 --> 00:07:31.250
But when he tries to kill someone in the spur of the moment like he did with me,

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:34.790
then the mix up might influence his actions.

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:40.540
That means that what drives
Kazuta to kill is feelings of love,

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:44.040
and behind his expressions of love is the drive to kill.

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:46.870
So he buries people alive?

00:07:46.870 --> 00:07:50.080
What kind of weirdo is this Kazuta Haruka?

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:43.200
Kaeru.

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:44.540
I remember.

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:46.580
My name is Sakaido.

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:49.700
Full name unknown,
but I'm the brilliant detective.

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:52.750
I will solve the mystery of her death.

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:55.160
Oh, I've got it.

00:08:55.160 --> 00:08:56.870
Hey, come on now!

00:08:56.870 --> 00:08:58.750
That's too fast!

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:06.700
Kaeru was killed by a single stab to the chest.

00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:08.910
The weapon is gone.

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:11.000
The killer must have taken it.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:15.200
Further, Kaeru lost a large amount of blood.

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:17.620
And it's pooled around her.

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:18.870
But.

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:21.000
Something's off about this.

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:23.580
If she was stabbed in this
weightless environment,

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:28.000
the blood should have
spattered in every direction.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:32.120
Instead, it's pooled flat around her.

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:35.910
And of course the blood couldn't
have floated up from the floor.

00:09:35.910 --> 00:09:39.370
If it had, the tatami mat would be stained.

00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:43.120
But the floor is clean, with no
indication blood was wiped away.

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:46.250
Kaeru was killed in mid-air,

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:50.950
and to keep the blood from
staining the floor or spraying all over,

00:09:50.950 --> 00:09:56.500
the killer carefully spread the blood out flat.

00:09:56.500 --> 00:09:58.290
But why?

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:04.330
To hide something beneath the canopy of blood.

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:06.120
Hello there.

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:10.410
Hello.

00:10:11.450 --> 00:10:12.500
This is...

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:14.500
Not one particular person.

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:18.870
The voice, eye colors, and mole
position are constantly changing.

00:10:18.870 --> 00:10:21.540
Breaking the pattern down.

00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:23.870
It's the Gravedigger's victims.

00:10:23.870 --> 00:10:27.450
Ayase Minami, Kouda Shiki, Yamashita Toshiki,

00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:32.160
Shiina Kaori, Masuda Kazuyuki,
and finally Mishima Kana.

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:35.750
All right. I hereby acknowledge
Kazuta Haruka as the Gravedigger.

00:10:35.750 --> 00:10:37.250
Secure an arrest warrant.

00:10:37.250 --> 00:10:39.500
The house has been identified.

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:44.000
It's a detached building on the grounds
of Kazuta Haruka's family home.

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:46.370
Both it and the main house are empty,

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:49.450
but there's a brewery for
soy sauce on the grounds.

00:10:49.450 --> 00:10:52.370
Do you think what the Gravedigger traps his victims inside

00:10:52.370 --> 00:10:56.500
isn't a coffin, but a fermentation barrel?

00:10:57.450 --> 00:10:59.080
Got the address.

00:10:59.080 --> 00:11:00.910
Ms. Nishimura is near there.

00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:02.200
You heard her.

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:03.750
Can you handle it?

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:05.660
I'm on my way.

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:10.830
What are you doing down here?

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:14.250
I'm the brilliant detective. Think.

00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:18.700
I wonder, is the killer hiding you from someone?

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:21.910
There's a super scary monster.

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:24.450
Where is it now?

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:27.000
I don't know.

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:32.410
Then where is the person
who killed Kaeru-- is this girl?

00:11:32.410 --> 00:11:35.000
I don't know that either.

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:40.120
But I think he's probably
out fighting that monster.

00:11:40.120 --> 00:11:42.200
I see.

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:45.250
Sit tight there for a while longer, okay?

00:11:45.250 --> 00:11:46.700
Okay.

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:49.580
What can I use as a weapon?

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:51.870
So that's the best I've got.

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:56.750
What's this?

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:58.200
Piece the picture together.

00:11:58.200 --> 00:11:59.410
Yes, ma'am.

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:04.000
It's from Kazuta's final year of middle school.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:07.000
When Kazuta was considered
a victim of the Perforator,

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:11.290
the investigators found the same
picture when they searched his room.

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:13.790
It's a memory of an actual possession.

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:17.830
Thoroughly check the people in the picture, too.

00:12:17.830 --> 00:12:21.700
If feelings of love truly
drive the Gravedigger to kill,

00:12:21.700 --> 00:12:24.250
the person he loves might be in it.

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:34.700
A middle-school classmate?

00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:39.910
Love, not the drive to kill, serves
as the impulse for Kazuta to kill,

00:12:39.910 --> 00:12:45.080
and he's been publicly sending snuff
films to the person he has feelings for.

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:48.580
But could he really go so far on impulse alone?

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:52.790
With just a little thought, he should realize what he's doing is crazy.

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:55.160
Kazuta has a hole in his head, right?

00:12:55.160 --> 00:12:59.750
He might have damage to other brain functions, not just his unconscious.

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:01.450
Good point.

00:13:01.450 --> 00:13:04.870
But what about the object of his affections?

00:13:04.870 --> 00:13:08.370
What would he do if that person was killed?

00:13:08.370 --> 00:13:10.830
It's not his fault that he became this way.

00:13:10.830 --> 00:13:14.910
Who knows. But let's send
that picture to the other officers.

00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:17.000
Yes, sir.

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:20.250
Can I choose which one to visit?

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:22.580
Sure. Pick the cutest one, though.

00:13:22.580 --> 00:13:24.200
Yeah, yeah.

00:13:29.750 --> 00:13:33.040
I mean, is the Wakumusubi even going to react?

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:36.000
Hondomachi got a kiss because she's a girl...

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:38.830
Wait, maybe the gender doesn't matter...

00:13:56.950 --> 00:13:59.830
Director Momoki, it's John Walker!

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:13.250
So it's him!

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:17.540
You bastard!

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:35.450
Dammit!

00:14:35.450 --> 00:14:37.500
Who the hell was that?

00:14:39.540 --> 00:14:42.000
We found barrels at the brewery.

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:44.080
Cords are coming out of them.

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:47.080
The previous victims might be in them.

00:14:47.080 --> 00:14:51.330
Or he might be in the middle of
recording new victims like Oono.

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:53.160
Any reaction on the Wakumusubi?

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:54.410
None, sir.

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:55.660
Can you open them?

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:57.250
We'll try now.

00:14:57.250 --> 00:14:58.830
Be cautious.

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:00.000
Roger.

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:06.500
The sound just dies.

00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:08.660
They're filled with something.

00:15:08.660 --> 00:15:11.540
The lids are shut tight, too.

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:12.870
Any signals?

00:15:12.870 --> 00:15:14.660
Still analyzing.

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:18.660
Hey! Is somebody in there?

00:15:20.410 --> 00:15:23.450
Nishimura, stay vigilant of the surroundings.

00:15:23.450 --> 00:15:24.830
I know.

00:15:24.830 --> 00:15:26.830
Coming!

00:15:26.830 --> 00:15:28.540
Who might you be?

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:30.410
Oh, sorry.

00:15:30.410 --> 00:15:32.160
We're with the police.

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:35.120
May we ask you some questions?

00:15:43.870 --> 00:15:46.910
The boy was killed.

00:15:46.910 --> 00:15:48.700
Then...

00:15:48.700 --> 00:15:52.160
Will you protect me in his place?

00:16:00.200 --> 00:16:02.410
Do you hear me? Hello!

00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:04.500
It's no use. It's too tough!

00:16:06.250 --> 00:16:08.700
Sir, no luck with the signals.

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:11.250
They're too heavily encrypted.

00:16:11.250 --> 00:16:13.450
They'll take time to analyze.

00:16:15.540 --> 00:16:17.620
Cut the power cables.

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:25.200
Huh? Soy sauce?

00:16:25.200 --> 00:16:27.540
No! It's gasoline!

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:29.910
What happened?

00:16:31.910 --> 00:16:33.830
Everybody out!

00:16:35.250 --> 00:16:37.450
Retreat!

00:16:37.450 --> 00:16:40.120
Even with this trap set, there's no drive to kill!

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:42.750
The Gravedigger did this, Momoki!

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:50.910
Shit!

00:16:50.910 --> 00:16:52.040
Stay back!

00:16:52.040 --> 00:16:53.950
There might be other traps!

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:57.040
Prepare a rescue!

00:16:59.910 --> 00:17:03.790
So, Ms. Inami you've been
here three times in total.

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:06.790
Once at age 13, and twice at 14.

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:08.450
Is that right?

00:17:08.450 --> 00:17:12.750
I'm glad to get to meet someone
he was pretty close to.

00:17:14.080 --> 00:17:16.450
Excuse me for a moment.

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:21.290
Um, were there any other girls
who were close with Mr. Kazuta?

00:17:21.290 --> 00:17:26.290
Or perhaps someone with
a special romantic connection?

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:27.620
Is something wrong?

00:17:27.620 --> 00:17:33.250
No, forgive me. Ms. Hondomachi, was it?

00:17:33.250 --> 00:17:35.000
What an unusual name.

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:36.660
I guess.

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:40.120
Um, is your injury okay?

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:41.950
Oh, I'm sorry!

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:48.250
It's fine now, but there are still some
areas that open up when I move around.

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:50.870
It must look unpleasant. My apologies.

00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:53.290
Not at all.

00:17:53.290 --> 00:17:55.410
There, all cleaned up.

00:17:55.410 --> 00:17:57.500
Oh, thanks.

00:17:58.910 --> 00:18:01.700
Um... Thank you very much.

00:18:01.700 --> 00:18:04.120
No problem.

00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:06.250
Back to Kazuta.

00:18:06.250 --> 00:18:09.620
It really didn't feel like he was dating someone,

00:18:09.620 --> 00:18:12.200
and I've never heard anything about it,

00:18:12.200 --> 00:18:15.830
so I think maybe he never dated anyone.

00:18:15.830 --> 00:18:18.290
At least, not during middle school.

00:18:18.290 --> 00:18:19.910
Is that so?

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:23.040
But maybe he <i>was </i>dating someone.

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:24.660
Say, you, Ms. Inami?

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:27.580
Me? That's impossible.

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:31.200
It didn't feel like we were that close at all.

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:35.540
Even when I was invited over,
it was always with friends.

00:18:35.540 --> 00:18:38.120
Then you were just friends?

00:18:38.120 --> 00:18:44.580
Hmm. I guess we were
something more... distant than that.

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:46.500
Oh, I see.

00:18:46.500 --> 00:18:51.000
Then you had no interest, in the romantic sense.

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:52.370
Right.

00:18:53.620 --> 00:18:59.500
But you did acquire information
on whether he was dating someone.

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:04.000
That's not something you do
if you're not interested, is it.

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:08.950
Oh, you're good, officer. You caught me!

00:19:08.950 --> 00:19:11.540
So tell me. What was the situation, really?

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:13.080
Oh?

00:19:14.870 --> 00:19:19.000
You see, we really never dated or anything.

00:19:19.000 --> 00:19:22.120
But I'm sure you understand
what it's like, Ms. Hondomachi.

00:19:22.120 --> 00:19:26.000
For there to be someone who
might like you. That kind of thing.

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:29.450
Actually, I'm a little oblivious.

00:19:30.700 --> 00:19:35.370
No girl could be as cute as you are and not notice such things.

00:19:35.370 --> 00:19:39.080
No, I'm really not as cute as I seem to be.

00:19:39.080 --> 00:19:41.580
Though my situation wasn't as bad as it is now.

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:46.290
In the end, what makes
girls cute isn't how they look.

00:19:46.290 --> 00:19:48.410
You're still very cute.

00:19:48.410 --> 00:19:50.950
I appreciate your words,

00:19:50.950 --> 00:19:55.870
but girls' standards for a cute girl
differ from boys' standards, don't they.

00:19:58.040 --> 00:20:01.290
But you really <i>are </i>cute.

00:20:01.290 --> 00:20:04.500
Um, returning to business...

00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:09.370
It's rude of me to ask, but you're
unmarried, aren't you, Ms. Inami?

00:20:09.370 --> 00:20:10.830
That's right.

00:20:10.830 --> 00:20:14.580
Do you have a boyfriend or anything like that?

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:16.540
Are you interested in me?

00:20:16.540 --> 00:20:20.330
What? Oh, no, no. That's not what I meant.

00:20:20.330 --> 00:20:22.870
I know you're just investigating a case.

00:20:22.870 --> 00:20:26.330
Of course that's not your interest in me.

00:20:26.330 --> 00:20:28.950
Just a joke, of course.

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:30.500
A boyfriend, huh.

00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:32.040
Nope.

00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:36.200
Have you... ever had one?

00:20:36.200 --> 00:20:39.950
Wow. I'm amazed you can pry so hard.

00:20:39.950 --> 00:20:44.040
It's my job to be curious. I'm sorry.

00:20:44.040 --> 00:20:46.580
It's related to the investigation?

00:20:47.330 --> 00:20:49.200
I'm not sure.

00:20:49.200 --> 00:20:51.250
A boyfriend, huh.

00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:55.580
Well, I <i>am </i>27, so of course I've had one, but...

00:20:55.580 --> 00:20:58.000
Hey, there's been an emergency. Time to go.

00:20:58.000 --> 00:20:59.410
Almost done.

00:20:59.410 --> 00:21:00.950
What?

00:21:00.950 --> 00:21:02.580
Are you sure?

00:21:02.580 --> 00:21:03.750
Yes.

00:21:03.750 --> 00:21:07.540
You've had a boyfriend, but
not someone you've truly loved?

00:21:07.540 --> 00:21:11.620
You're good. I suppose
you could put it that way.

00:21:11.620 --> 00:21:14.330
The reason you didn't love your boyfriend is

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:19.790
because you loved Kazuta Haruka. Isn't that right?

00:21:19.790 --> 00:21:22.540
What? That's ridiculous!

00:21:24.040 --> 00:21:25.700
Wait. Maybe not.

00:21:25.700 --> 00:21:27.080
Hondomachi, hurry.

00:21:27.080 --> 00:21:28.330
Understood.

00:21:28.330 --> 00:21:30.250
Then, one last question.

00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:35.410
Is there some blood coming from my wound again?

00:21:35.410 --> 00:21:36.580
Not at all.

00:21:36.580 --> 00:21:40.040
Oh, forgive me. I shouldn't be staring.

00:21:40.040 --> 00:21:41.290
Not a problem.

00:21:41.290 --> 00:21:42.370
Um...

00:21:42.370 --> 00:21:44.040
Yes?

00:21:44.040 --> 00:21:45.330
Is it possible--

00:21:45.330 --> 00:21:46.410
I mean,

00:21:46.410 --> 00:21:47.410
I already know.

00:21:47.410 --> 00:21:51.290
You enjoy wounds and
watching people die, don't you?

00:21:52.750 --> 00:21:55.660
Allow me to fill you in on something.

00:21:55.660 --> 00:21:59.370
Kazuta Haruka and I kissed.

00:22:00.330 --> 00:22:01.660
You two haven't, right?

00:22:01.660 --> 00:22:05.910
I mean, your relationship
was only platonic and sticky.

00:22:05.910 --> 00:22:07.120
What?

00:22:07.120 --> 00:22:09.000
Who could have imagined?

00:22:09.000 --> 00:22:13.700
His scrambled romantic and
murderous urges didn't conflict at all.

00:22:13.700 --> 00:22:15.830
Freeze! Put your hands up!

00:22:15.830 --> 00:22:20.120
Get up slowly, turn toward me,
and get on your knees!

00:22:20.120 --> 00:22:22.000
Hey! What's going on?

00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:23.080
What's with the gun?

00:22:23.080 --> 00:22:25.250
I took a page from your book.

00:22:25.250 --> 00:22:28.040
Also, she's the Gravedigger.

00:22:28.040 --> 00:22:31.450
What?! Isn't Kazuta the Gravedigger?

00:22:31.450 --> 00:22:35.450
The murders Kazuta committed were for her!

00:22:35.450 --> 00:22:38.870
They were presents for this sadist!

00:22:38.870 --> 00:22:42.160
Inami Nahoshi, where is Kazuta Haruka?

00:24:19.870 --> 00:24:23.290
It's a pity your boyfriend died.

00:24:23.290 --> 00:24:26.250
Not really. He wasn't my boyfriend.

00:24:26.250 --> 00:24:29.370
But he loved you, didn't he?

00:24:29.370 --> 00:24:31.620
Don't say that.

00:24:32.620 --> 00:24:37.120
<i>He </i>should be the one to say that.

00:24:38.620 --> 00:24:40.620
You're right.
